:"toolu_01SiDYomCCx1FHz8h4A4DZ4r","tool_input":{"command":"ls ~/Workspace/ 2>/dev/null; echo \"---\"; cd ~/Workspace/Spotify 2>/dev/null && bd show spot-2ig --json 2>&1 | head -50","description":"Check spot-2ig in Spotify repo"}},{"tool_name":"Bash","tool_use_id":"toolu_01P6FgkD8QgBX42AtSVVw1JV","tool_input":{"command":"ls /home/drspeedracer/Workspace/","description":"List workspace"}},{"tool_name":"Bash","tool_use_id":"toolu_013b1Ztx287SfTdKiXEN9xrq","tool_input":{"command":"grep -rn \"flywheel/roster\\|roster.json\" .claude/settings.json .claude/*.json 2>/dev/null; echo \"=== deny block ===\"; python3 -c \"\nimport json,sys\nd=json.load(open('.claude/settings.json'))\nprint(json.dumps(d.get('permissions',{}),indent=1)[:4000])\n\" 2>/dev/null || cat .claude/settings.json"}},{"tool_name":"Bash","tool_use_id":"toolu_012axwHjFLH846Z9iM4eKS2D","tool_input":{"command":"python3 -c \"\nimport json;d=json.load(open('/home/drspeedracer/Workspace/agentic-flywheel-fw-ojk/.flywheel/roster.json'))\nprint([ (r.get('name'), r.get('default_branch')) for r in d.get('repos',[]) ])\"","description":"Check roster repos for default_branch"}},{"tool_name":"Bash","tool_use_id":"toolu_01VP3U3KyrXuzfJVqW2G45kf","tool_input":{"command":"bd list --status open --json 2>&1 | head -5; echo \"---\"; gh repo view jamesponwith/agentic-flywheel --json defaultBranchRef 2>&1 | head -5","description":"Check open beads and default branch"}},{"tool_name":"Bash","tool_use_id":"toolu_01HxEpu4FjeQkqVFFkU45tZC","tool_input":{"command":"gh repo view jamesponwith/agentic-flywheel --json defaultBranchRef 2>&1 | head -5","description":"Check default branch via gh"}},{"tool_name":"Bash","tool_use_id":"toolu_01LaCaCYL73XVaJEiS27bnr1","tool_input":{"command":"gh pr list --repo jamesponwith/agentic-flywheel --state all --limit 200 --json number,state,title,headRefName,baseRefName 2>&1 | python3 -c \"\nimport json,sys\nprs=json.load(sys.stdin)\nfor p in prs:\n    if p['state']=='MERGED' and p['baseRefName']!='main':\n        print(p['number'], p['state'], p['headRefName'], '->', p['baseRefName'], '|', p['title'][:60])\nprint('total', len(prs))\n\"","description":"List merged PRs with non-main base"}}],"terminal_reason":"completed","fast_mode_state":"off","fast_mode_disabled_reason":"sdk_opt_in_required","subagent_stats":{"spawned":3,"requested":{"background":0,"foreground":3,"unset":0},"started_in_background":0,"max_depth":1,"spawned_by_subagents":0,"completed":3,"failed":0,"killed":{"parent":0,"user":0,"system":0},"refused":{"depth_limit":0,"concurrency_limit":0,"budget":0},"by_type":{"Explore":3}},"is_error":false,"num_turns":130,"subtype":"success","api_error_status":null,"result":"**fw-ojk — PR #79 open, gate green.**\n\n`reconcile-board` closed beads on `gh`'s `MERGED`, which means \"merged somewhere\". Now a merge counts only onto the repo's default branch, asked of `gh repo view`; a PR merged elsewhere is reported as `merged-elsewhere` with the branch it went to and never closes.\n\n**Two places I went past the design note:**\n\n- The design said \"default branch from the roster or gh\". All three review lenses attacked the roster half — no repo sets it, its justification is impossible (`ghPRs` asks gh about that repo one line later), and one JSON line reinstates this exact bug. `Repo.DefaultBranch` is now `json:\"-\"`, gh-resolved only.\n- Acceptance criterion 3 (\"re-running surfaces spot-2ig\") can't be met by the forward fix — spot-2ig is *already closed*, and the reconciler only scanned open beads. It now also reports `closed-elsewhere`, gated on a detour PR existing so healthy repos pay no extra `bd` call. Reports, never reopens.\n\n**What I could not verify:** running `fleet reconcile-board` against the workspace. `gh` invocations and the other repos' paths are both outside this session's sandbox, so the `closed-elsewhere` path that surfaces spot-2ig is unit-tested only. Worth one manual run before merging — it's flagged as an unchecked box in the PR body.\n\n**Review:** 16 findings, 3 lenses, all in `.flywheel/review.jsonl` — 13 accepted (including three the panel caught that I'd have shipped: a `MERGED` PR with no base silently closing nothing, a small main-bound PR overriding a detour, and PR titles reaching the committed digest unflattened), 2 rejected with reasons, 1 deferred to **fw-64x** (`reconcile.go` and `bypass.go` still hardcode `main..`; three helpers hardcode the owner).\n\nGate: build, vet, full suite and the 160s conformance suite green; pre-commit clean on all four commits, nothing bypassed. Weight `w:2`. Bead left open and in progress. Ran solo per `run-context.json`, so no registration or reservation.","ttft_ms":1515,"type":"result","duration_ms":1562081,"uuid":"a687183d-1caf-491a-a62f-bcc4c9479ce9","ttft_stream_ms":970,"time_to_request_ms":113,"queued_turn_count":0}
